"""Explains layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3464: a 'time, age and version' detector.

The component reads the current word and the word before it. It goes clearly
negative on the nouns that name a span of time, an age, a version or a stage
("years", "version", "generations", "stage", "decades", "history", "date") and
most strongly when such a noun follows a recency or age word ("recent years",
"future version", "latest version", "newer version", "early stage"). It is also
strongly negative on "old" in "N years old" (and on "-old" as in "32-year-old").
Weaker signals: a positive response to the end-of-thinking token "</think>", and a
small positive response to a few forward-looking words ("after", "before",
"coming", "near"). Everything else predicts 0, so most of the variance it leaves
unexplained is diffuse, word-specific noise.
