"""A lexical mixture, dominated by a negative response to 'instance'.
Instances, institutions and images are negative; responsibility/burden and
list introductions are positive.  'For instance' weakens the instance cue;
'of' immediately after a recognized noun retains part of its signal.
Explicit CJK character cues capture additional, disparate responses.
Unlisted words and longer-range context are deliberately left at zero.
