"""Approximate a mixed lexical feature for error words and code notation.

Most tokens predict zero. Negative cues include literal error words and
suffixes, comments, namespaces, ampersands, brackets, source suffixes and
named code/error-related word classes. A 512-character lookback distinguishes
code/indentation from links and TeX. JSON openings are also negative; two
control tags and a document-initial hash have small positive responses.
Context resets at every document boundary. Unlisted lexical variation is
intentionally left unexplained rather than memorized in a token table.
