"""Superscript/exponent detector, strongest at the first exponent digit.

Literal raised digits get a negative response. For caret notation, opening
brackets, signs and spaces weaken the response; subsequent digits fade.
Trigonometric powers, numeral bases and raised Lean identifier suffixes
are stronger. Caret runs/eyes, textual .sup. markup, subscripts, roots and
the words squared/cubed have smaller responses. Other text gets zero.
